{"title":"Jadhav Arithmetic Merging Equation","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Jadhav_Arithmetic_Merging_Equation.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/2/27/Jadhav_Arithmetic_Merging_Equation.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"591\" height=\"96\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption>Jadhav Arithmetic Merging Equation</figcaption></figure>\n<p><b>Jadhav Arithmetic Merging Equation</b> or <b>Jadhav's Summation</b> is a formula which can do summation of a finite arithmetic series whose terms are the result of product of respective terms of two arithmetic series with constant common difference (arithmetic progression). Derived by  <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jyotiraditya_Jadhav&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Jyotiraditya Jadhav (page does not exist)\">Jyotiraditya Jadhav</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Derivation_and_Statement\">Derivation and Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jadhav_Arithmetic_Merging_Equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Derivation and Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us consider two different arithmetic progression series.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c5c685abd447091e6be8c42a42bc08c8ba12ff0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a , a+d , a+2d , a+3d ... a+(n-1)d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"288\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3aebdd406652482b07cb172a057202e58405b33e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 , a_1+d_1 , a_1+2d_1 , a_1+3d_1 ... a_1+(n-1)d_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Now the series formed by product of their respective terms will be\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa14d61a5fe806b878386d09cc46b691b5ed08a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$aa_1 ,(a+d)(a_1+d_1) ,(a+2d)(a_1+2d_1),(a+3d)(a_1+3d_1) ...[a+(n-1)] a_1+(n-1)d_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"688\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>So the summation of all the terms will be\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f192b12d97a39c637f1425f7b1d4cfd14381ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Sigma a_1+(a+d)(a_1+d_1) ...+[a+(n-1)d][a_1+(n-1)d_1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"444\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Giving the <b>Jadhav Arithmetic Merging Equation</b> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317a4d89e6336432b71e2e8a5634f171995b4b1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(a_1a)+d_1d \\frac{(n-1)(n)(2n-1)}{6}+[{a_1d+ad_1}]\\frac{(n-1)n}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"428\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Nomenclature\">Nomenclature</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jadhav_Arithmetic_Merging_Equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Nomenclature\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><b>n&#160;: Total number of terms in the corresponding series</b></li>\n<li><b>a&#160;: First term of first series</b></li>\n<li><b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />&#160;: First term of second series</b></li>\n<li><b>d&#160;: Common difference of first series</b></li>\n<li><b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/44612d9d6ec37da7f4edd0f205d65cdac5954dc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />: Common difference of second series</b></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jadhav_Arithmetic_Merging_Equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: History\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Been known Jyotiraditya Jadhav was trying to find a generalized formula to easily apply <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factorial\" title=\"Factorial\">Factorial</a> to any number which was as superior as <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binomial_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Binomial theorem\">Binomial_theorem</a> and came across a situation of multivariate binomials and was necessary to find their product to complete Factorial Equation and so started finding direct <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"//www.ck12.org/book/ck-12-middle-school-math-concepts-grade-7/section/1.2\">[1]</a> to complete it but was pretty unsuccessful in it and hence started with algebraic patterns and made Jadhav Arithmetic Merging Equation overnight.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"background:#ffdddd; width:60%; border:2px solid #aa0000; margin:auto; text-align:center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"padding:10px;\">\n<p><b>This page has been proposed for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_Wiki:Deletion_policy\" title=\"AoPS Wiki:Deletion policy\">deletion</a>.</b> Reason: <b>theorem is not well-known</b>\n</p>\n<hr style=\"border:1px solid #aa0000;\" />\n<p><small>\n<b>Note to sysops:</b> Before deleting, please review: • <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special:WhatLinksHere/Jadhav_Arithmetic_Merging_Equation\" title=\"Special:WhatLinksHere/Jadhav Arithmetic Merging Equation\">What links here</a> • <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Talk:Jadhav_Arithmetic_Merging_Equation&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Talk:Jadhav Arithmetic Merging Equation (page does not exist)\">Discussion page</a> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Jadhav_Arithmetic_Merging_Equation&amp;action=history\">Edit history</a>\n</small>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234317\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 55/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 887/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 25/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1488/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.339      1 Template:Delete\n100.00%    8.339      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21501:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234317 and revision id 290893. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}